# Spotler Message Product Context Skill

## Purpose

Use this Skill when designing or redesigning product features for Spotler Message.

This Skill gives Figma Make product context for Spotler Message so it can make better UX and product decisions without starting from generic messaging, helpdesk, chatbot, or SaaS assumptions. It explains what the product is, who uses it, how it works, which workflows matter, which terminology to use, and what product logic should be preserved.

This is not a Design System Skill. Do not use this Skill for visual styling, component rules, typography, spacing, colours, or layout patterns. Use the separate Spotler Design System Skill or attached design system documentation for those decisions.

---

## Product Summary

Spotler Message is a messaging platform for managing one-to-one customer conversations and proactive messaging campaigns through WhatsApp for Business and other messaging channels.

It helps organisations manage customer conversations from one central inbox, automate routine interactions, route conversations to the right people, send proactive updates or campaigns, and maintain compliance when using channels such as WhatsApp.

Spotler Message supports both:

- Human one-to-one conversations
- Automated chatbot or guided flow conversations
- Proactive messaging campaigns and notifications

The product is especially useful for customer service, marketing, sales, HR, recruitment, retail, travel, automotive, public sector, and other teams that want to scale direct customer communication while keeping it personal, fast, compliant, and manageable.

---

## Core Problem Spotler Message Solves

Customers increasingly expect fast, personal communication through channels they use every day, especially WhatsApp.

Traditional channels such as email and phone often struggle with:

- Long response times
- High service volumes
- Repetitive questions
- Missed or unanswered messages
- Poor overview across channels
- Limited conversation history
- Lack of routing or ownership
- Difficulty using WhatsApp compliantly
- Limited automation
- Poor collaboration between team members
- Low visibility for urgent notifications or time-sensitive campaigns

Spotler Message solves this by bringing messaging channels into one central, compliant platform where teams can manage conversations, automate repetitive flows, send approved messages, and measure response and conversation performance.

The product makes WhatsApp and other messaging channels manageable as strategic service, engagement, and conversion channels.

---

## Why Conversational Messaging Matters

Conversational messaging is important because customers increasingly prefer direct, accessible, mobile-first communication.

WhatsApp and similar messaging channels are used daily and often receive much higher engagement than traditional channels such as email. WhatsApp messages can have very high open rates, often above 90%, making them valuable for urgent updates, service communication, reminders, promotions, and conversion-focused follow-up.

For organisations, messaging is not only a support channel. It can also be used for:

- Customer service
- Notifications
- Campaigns
- Promotions
- Lead follow-up
- Conversion
- Recruitment
- Reminders
- Order or booking updates
- Event communication

Designs should treat messaging as fast, direct, personal, permission-based, and operationally sensitive.

---

## Target Users and User Roles

Spotler Message is used by teams that manage direct customer communication through messaging channels.

### Primary users

#### Customer service agent

A customer service agent handles incoming conversations from WhatsApp, SMS, webchat, social messaging, or other channels.

Goals:

- Respond quickly
- Keep conversations organised
- Avoid missed messages
- See conversation history
- Use templates where appropriate
- Hand over or escalate conversations when needed

Typical needs:

- Shared inbox
- Conversation status
- Assignment
- Labels
- Notes
- Routing
- Contact history
- Channel context

---

#### Customer service team lead

A team lead manages workload, assignments, response times, and team performance.

Goals:

- Distribute conversations across team members
- Reduce response times
- Monitor workload
- Ensure consistent handling
- Prevent duplicate work
- Improve service quality

Typical needs:

- Team inbox overview
- Assignment controls
- Routing rules
- Response-time reporting
- Conversation volume insights
- Team performance dashboards

---

#### Marketing campaign manager

A marketing campaign manager uses messaging channels for campaigns, promotions, announcements, and time-sensitive communication.

Goals:

- Send approved WhatsApp campaigns
- Reach customers with high-visibility messages
- Use consent-based messaging
- Personalise campaign content
- Measure engagement and response

Typical needs:

- Approved WhatsApp templates
- Broadcast messaging
- Audience or contact selection
- Rich media support
- Campaign performance reports
- Compliance guidance

---

#### Sales or lead follow-up user

A sales or lead follow-up user uses messaging to respond quickly to interest from forms, events, or campaigns.

Goals:

- Follow up leads faster
- Start direct conversations
- Improve conversion
- Use WhatsApp after form submissions or event interactions
- Maintain context across touchpoints

Typical needs:

- Triggered conversations
- Contact history
- CRM integration
- Conversation assignment
- Templates
- Handover from automation to human

---

#### HR or recruitment user

An HR or recruitment user uses messaging to communicate quickly with candidates, applicants, or employees.

Goals:

- Reach people faster than email
- Coordinate interviews or reminders
- Answer common questions
- Improve response rates
- Keep communication accessible

Typical needs:

- Messaging templates
- Contact-level history
- Shared inbox
- Automation for common questions
- Notifications and reminders

---

### Secondary users

#### Automation or chatbot manager

An automation user configures chatbots, guided flows, FAQs, routing, and human handover.

Goals:

- Reduce repetitive workload
- Automate common questions
- Route conversations correctly
- Ensure smooth handover to agents
- Maintain a personal customer experience

Typical needs:

- Flow builder
- Knowledge base
- FAQ automation
- AI-powered chatbot configuration
- Trigger-based routing
- Handover logic

---

#### Compliance or operations user

A compliance or operations user ensures that messaging is used securely and within permission and channel rules.

Goals:

- Maintain GDPR-friendly processes
- Use WhatsApp Business officially
- Respect consent and permissions
- Maintain audit trail
- Control user access

Typical needs:

- Permission-based messaging
- Audit trail
- User roles
- WhatsApp Business API approval status
- Template approval status
- European hosting context

---

#### Integration specialist

An integration specialist connects Spotler Message with CRM systems, APIs, webhooks, connector platforms, or other Spotler products.

Goals:

- Synchronise contacts
- Record conversations at contact level
- Trigger messages from external events
- Connect service, marketing, and sales workflows
- Automate data exchange

Typical needs:

- API and webhook configuration
- CRM integration
- Zapier or Make integration
- Spotler ecosystem connections
- Sync status

